nimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3618291660","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113609#issuecomment-3618291660","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113609","id":3618291660,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Xqr_M","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T19:32:45Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T19:32:45Z","body":"> @clayjohn\r\n> \r\n> https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/05830dfbfb60a32c7757240cb152d4b03ffba1a1/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/environment/sky.cpp#L1108-L1118\r\n> \r\n> https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/05830dfbfb60a32c7757240cb152d4b03ffba1a1/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/environment/sky.cpp#L1262-L1263\r\n> \r\n> It looks like the when the directional light buffer is updated, so is the radiance buffer?\r\n\r\nThanks, that's right. But the radiance buffer should only be updated if the directional light buffer is updated **and** the sky shader is using directional lights. So I think the proper solution will be to change when the radiance is set to dirty\r\n\r\nI.e. this: \r\n```\r\nif (sky) { \r\n\tsky->reflection.dirty = true; \r\n} \r\n```\r\n\r\nShould look like:\r\n```\r\nif (sky && sky->uses_lights) { \r\n\tsky->reflection.dirty = true; \r\n} \r\n```\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3618291660/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3618346956","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113609#issuecomment-3618346956","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113609","id":3618346956,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Xq5fM","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T19:45:54Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T19:45:54Z","body":"@clayjohn If you go up a bit, this code is already dependent on: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/dec5a373d97cbadce5e1fabe6095ae9957ff3aa6/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/environment/sky.cpp#L1028 If sun scatter is enabled, lights appear in the sky even if the user's shader does not use any `LIGHTX_*` built-ins (`uses_lights` will be `false`). Is this not the same reason for using `SKY_MODE_INCREMENTAL` when `uses_lights == true`?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3618346956/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3618465957","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113609#issuecomment-3618465957","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113609","id":3618465957,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XrWil","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T20:21:08Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T20:21:08Z","body":"> If sun scatter is enabled, lights appear in the sky even if the user's shader does not use any LIGHTX_* built-ins (uses_lights will be false). Is this not the same reason for using SKY_MODE_INCREMENTAL when uses_lights == true?\r\n\r\nGood point. I was forgetting that sun_scatter is evaluated in the sky shader. In my mind it was only in the scene shader and fog shader. In that case this is the correct fix!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3618465957/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3628338211","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113609#issuecomment-3628338211","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113609","id":3628338211,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YRAwj","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-08T18:01:39Z","updated_at":"2025-12-08T18:01:39Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/36